== plan (written before the run): the same harness with TONA_METAL_PIN=rset (all weight buffers in a residency set
   on the queue), twice, against the k = 2 servers above. Expectation: if the stall is residency of mapped pages,
   the first decode pass's stall falls under 50 ms; if a power state or scheduler effect, it stays 0.2 s.
   result: rset1 first waits 42.1 ms, then split 188.2 ms; rset2 48.9 and 179.6 ms (21.49 GB in the set): unchanged, not residency
== plan (written before the runs): prefill command buffers (TONA_METAL_CB_LOG=1 now also prints the GPU idle
   between a chunk's command buffers) and the stall against the prompt length (1000, 2000, 4000, 8000 tokens, 60
   decode tokens each, one server). Expectation: if the stall follows the length of the GPU load, it grows with it.
   result: longest stall of the first decode passes 25.3 / 22.1 / 57.6 / 78.7 ms (earlier lengths run: 16.7 / 18.9 /
   36.8 / 116.8), plus a first command buffer waiting up to 44 ms. Inside the prefill chunks the GPU idles 7 ms per
   146 command buffers (0.12 ms longest), except in the first chunk after a decode phase: 30 to 38 ms once.
   The server reports 2.6 GB free RAM and the load logs of the A/B runs about 12 GB compressed: our own buffers
   (state, KV, scratch; shared storage, not the mapped weights) that decode uses and the prefill does not sit
   unused for the length of the prefill, and the first decode pass waits until they are back.
== plan: probe TONA_METAL_PIN_OWN=1 (every buffer of Device::floats in a residency set on the queue; the weights
   stay out), the lengths run twice. Expectation: the stall goes under 5 ms if the cause is our own buffers.
   result: longest split 0.0 and 0.1 ms, longest first submit 0.5 and 0.2 ms over all lengths (against 78.7 and
   44.4 without); the 30 to 38 ms in the first prefill chunk after decode gone as well (once 8.5 ms in the first
   chunk of a fresh server). 8000-token prefill 48.7 and 49.4 s against 46.2 s (one request each, unchecked).
== plan: the agent case (the coordinator's question): the 8000-token prompt, then three tool steps, each the whole
   conversation plus the answer and a short tool result (prefix cache hit, about 36 new tokens), 3 s or 30 s between
